    Document how to create a service (#8147)
    
    Fixes #5410.
    
    Add a developer guide page that explains how to write an OSGi service
    from scratch: DS components and immediate, configuration with @Modified,
    REST endpoints, job producers, and why not to use ManagedService. The
    examples are taken from the hello-world and media inspection modules.
    
    Also fixes a couple minor things in the hello world example service.
    
    While looking at this I found `OsgiAbstractJobProducer`, which seems to
    be less boilerplatey version of `AbstractJobProducer`, but is only used
    in one example service. Is `OsgiAbstractJobProducer` something we should
    be using everywhere, should we get rid of it, any opinions? :D
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Compiling should be enough for the hello world modules, so this is
    mostly just reading.
    
